DFlash2 drafting for qwen3_5_moe checkpoints on CUDA (TensorFold 1.1.7).

Stock 1.1.7 drafts qwen3_5_moe only with the checkpoint's MTP layer read from an MLX mtp-4bit.safetensors; the DFlash2
drafter path (cuda_draft*.zig) exists for the dense qwen3_5 family on the same engine. Re-port of the earlier
ornith-1.5-122b-tensorfold recipe's patch for 1.1.1:
  - cuda_native_moe.zig: openDrafter opens a DFlash2 model when --drafter names a directory whose config.json has a
    dflash_config, and the MTP head otherwise (stock), behind one return type whose calibration step is optional;
  - native/cuda_drafted.zig: accepts that optional calibration step (null: nothing to calibrate, as for MTP before);
  - cuda_draft_config.zig: accepts a drafter trained with a block of 16 as well as 8 (incoai/Ornith-1.5-122B-DFlash2
    is 16; the rounds draft 16 positions either way, and the two-tap convolutions do not depend on the block).
Exactness is the engine's: drafted rows are verified by the target, so replies equal "draft": false (checked, README).

